                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Not exactly great, but I imagine this could be fun for small children. \n\nIt's nice that it's playble without the controllers. The idea is also fine. The graphics leave a lot to be desired, but I guess it wasn't exactly going for realism. The gameplay is repetitive but again, it doesn't feel like something aimed at adult audience. \n\nMy biggest complaint would be a certain debuff when eating a wrong bug - I'm begging you developers, please don't include prolonged agressively shaking screen in your vr games. It's not like with regular games, in vr this can cause a serious headache and makes for a terrible experience.\n\n5/10",
